====================================================================================================
READING IT
====================================================================================================
  THE THRESHOLD. v123 measured the shot noise already in w as rms 0.0075 at
  |D|=4 rising to 0.0214 at |D|=16. A truncation error under 0.0214 is
  invisible to the estimator - smaller than the error the weights carry.

  AND THE ONLY chi THAT COUNTS IS ONE WELL BELOW MAX RANK. At d=4 the
  middle cut has max rank 4, so chi=3 there is three-quarters of full and
  says nothing. An earlier run of this file stopped at d=4 and read chi=3,
  err 0.0066 as 'a sufficient chi exists' - that was reading full rank as
  structure. d=6 and d=8 have max rank 8 and 16, where a small chi is
  genuinely a claim.

      arm            d   max rank   chi*   chi*/max rank   verdict
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   UNREALIZABLE     4        4       4      1.00        near full
   UNREALIZABLE     6        8       8      1.00        near full
   UNREALIZABLE     8       16    none        n/a        full rank
   REALIZABLE       4        4       3      0.75        near full
   REALIZABLE       6        8       6      0.75        near full
   REALIZABLE       8       16    none        n/a        full rank

  NO LOW BOND DIMENSION AT d>=6 IN THE MEASURED VECTORS. Every arm needs
  a chi at or near the maximum rank of its cut.

  AND THE CONFOUND CHECK DECIDES WHAT THAT MEANS. Realizable arm at d=8,
  exact vs measured, largest gap 0.192:
      chi=4:  exact 0.093   measured 0.272
      chi=8:  exact 0.017   measured 0.115

  THE EXACT VECTOR IS LOW RANK AND THE MEASURED ONE IS NOT. So the
  structure is real and SHOT NOISE IS DESTROYING IT - noise is full rank
  and at d=8 it is ~0.088 per sample, larger than the signal's own tail.
  THE INTERNAL CONTROL CONFIRMS THE MECHANISM. The gap appears only where
  there is structure to destroy: the UNREALIZABLE arm at d=8 is exact
  0.246 vs measured 0.247 at chi=8 - no gap at all, because those vectors
  are genuinely full rank and noise cannot lower a rank that is already
  maximal. Realizable shows 0.017 vs 0.115 over the same cells.

  BUT THE MECHANISM CHANGES, AND THE CONCLUSION DOES NOT. Finish the
  arithmetic: the sufficient chi on the EXACT vector at d=8 is 8, which
  is half of max rank 16, and an MPS prep at chi=8 costs ~4*d*chi^2 =
  2048 gates against the exact prep's 2^d - 1 = 255. It is 8.0x WORSE.
  4*d*chi^2 < 2^d - 1 at chi=8 needs d >= 12, i.e. |D| >= 4096, where the
  budget gives well under one shot per sample.

  SO: the structure is REAL, WEAK, and BURIED - and even ungoverned by
  noise it would not pay for itself at any size the register can reach.
  v125's cap stands. What this file changes is the reason: not 'the
  weights are generic' but 'the structure is too weak to buy the prep,
  and shot noise removes what there is'. Those imply different next
  moves, which is why the distinction is worth the extra arm.

  SCOPE. d in (4, 6, 8), N_sys=3, efficient_su2 reps=1, 32768 shots, 3 seeds,
  10 epochs, CONTIGUOUS cuts only, estimate-driven descent, no noise model,
  no hardware. Contiguous cuts under the natural qubit order is the MPS
  question specifically; a permuted order or a tree tensor network could
  find structure this misses, and neither is tested.
